.repowise/
*.mcp.json

# --- Build outputs ---
frontend/dist/

# The whole build/ tree is reproducible, so none of it is tracked:
#   bin/                   build output
#   appicon.png            Wails asset
#   windows/icon.ico       copied from images/icon.ico by the preBuildHooks
#                          in wails.json on every build
#   windows/info.json      \ Wails writes these from embedded defaults when
#   windows/*.manifest     / absent (see buildassets.ReadFile); ours are
#                            byte-identical to those defaults
#
# CAUTION: build/windows/info.json and wails.exe.manifest are also the
# customisation point. The moment you edit one — requesting admin rights via
# requestedExecutionLevel, adding longPathAware, hard-coding version fields —
# it must be force-added (`git add -f`) or un-ignored here, or the change will
# live only on your machine and CI will silently build without it.
build/

# --- Dependencies ---
frontend/node_modules/

